# Weekly progress email

Plain text only. No bullets, no bold, no App/Admin headings. Deliver the full mail in chat so it can be copied.

## Layout

1. Intro (one line)
2. Blank line
3. `Week N` (number only — not “Week N – Progress Update”)
4. One task per line: `Task name - status` (optional detail in parentheses before the dash)
5. Blank line
6. `Tasks for week N+1:`
7. Next-week tasks, one per line, no status
8. Blank line
9. `Kind regards,` then `Vukasin` on the next line

## Status words (use only these)

- `completed`
- `in progress`
- `95% completed` (or another percent if he gives one)
- `waiting for review from the rest of the team`

Never write `done`.

## Canonical example (Week 36)

```
Here’s a quick overview of what I worked on last week, along with the current status of each task:

Week 36
Admin panel – promo code design - completed
Admin panel – finance - completed
Admin panel – notification - in progress
Admin panel – notification support - completed
Admin panel – content (support can handle all the texts and images that are changeable in the app, e.g. services, vaccines, information, etc.) - in progress

Tasks for week 37:
Admin panel – content
Admin panel – notification

Kind regards,
Vukasin
```

Next-week lines are only what he names — do not add “Keep working on admin panel” or other filler.

When he corrects wording, status, or layout, patch this example in the same turn. Do not invent tasks. Pull last week’s work from chats and Figma; ask if a status is unclear.
